title: "DNS Tool: Domain Security Audit Platform"
type: software
version: "26.46.15"
date-released: 2026-04-17
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19468134

abstract: >-
  DNS Tool is an open-core OSINT platform for RFC-compliant domain
  security analysis. It evaluates SPF, DKIM, DMARC, DANE/TLSA,
  DNSSEC, BIMI, MTA-STS, TLS-RPT, and CAA configurations using
  multi-factor geometric-mean confidence scoring aligned with
  ICD 203 to produce structured security intelligence outputs.
  Each scan emits a 15-file deliverable bundle (engineer report,
  executive brief, observed-records snapshot, analysis history,
  discovered-subdomain inventory, integrity checksum, remediation
  plan, sources & methodology, and more), suitable for direct
  ingestion by retrieval agents such as DEVONagent. Independent
  scientific provenance is established by automated submission
  of every analysis to the Internet Archive (Wayback Machine).

